		<DeletedComponentTemplates />
		<Id>264</Id>
		<Name>Windows UDP Ephemeral Port Exhaustion</Name>
		<IsMockTemplate>false</IsMockTemplate>
		<Description>Watches the UDP dynamic port range on a Windows host: percent of the range in use and the processes holding it (PowerShell over WinRM), plus the native UDPv4 and TCPv4 counters that show a burst as it happens. Two Windows Event Log components turn Down the poll after System / Tcpip / 4266 (UDP) or 4231 (TCP) lands; see docs/modules/sam-udp-port-exhaustion-template.md.

Prerequisites: WinRM must be installed and properly configured on the target server.

Credentials: Administrator on the target server with domain/host part in username (domain\user).</Description>
		<Tags>
			<TagInfo>
				<Name>UDP</Name>
				<TemplateID>264</TemplateID>
			</TagInfo>
			<TagInfo>
				<Name>PowerShell</Name>
				<TemplateID>264</TemplateID>
			</TagInfo>
